# Herwig 7.2 cluster hadronization tune for Belle II
# e+e- -> qqbar continuum events
#
# This file is injected into the Herwig .in file just before 'run',
# overriding any template defaults.
# Format: standard Herwig 'set' commands, one per line.
#
# Parameters description reference, table 7.5 in Bellm et al., "The Physics of Herwig 7", arXiv:2512.16645 (2025)
# Note: Herwig 7.3.0 retuned several defaults; where they differ from the Herwig 7.2.0 values.
#
# Herwig 7.2 defaults are in:
#   share/Herwig/defaults/Hadronization.in  (Herwig 7.2.0 is available in the basf2 externals since version v02-04-00)

##################################################
# Example:
# Strange quark suppression; cluster fission and cluster decay
# Weight for selecting strange quark-antiquark pairs popped from the vacuum.
#
# Range: [0, 10]
# Herwig 7.2 default: 0.291717  (Note Herwig 7.3 default: 0.37)
# Effect: increase -> higher K/(K+pi) ratio (more K+/-, K0 from fission and decay).
#         decrease -> lower K/(K+pi) ratio (fewer K; more pi+/-/pi0).
##################################################
set /Herwig/Hadronization/HadronSelector:PwtSquark 0.291717

